// pfodWeb NOTE: per-board override — this is the ESP32-S3 USB-OTG dev
// board. Removed from the chip-level default chipGpios map:
//  33,34,35,36,37,38  onboard microSD card (SDMMC/SPI)
//  4,5,6,7,8,9        onboard 240x240 ST7789 LCD (DC/CS/CLK/MOSI/RST/BL)
//  12,13,17,18        USB dual-role power/mode control lines
//                     (DEV_VBUS_EN/BOOST_EN/LIMIT_EN/USB_HOST_EN)
// Kept: buttons (0,10,11,14), status LEDs (15,16), overcurrent flag
// (21), voltage monitors (1,2), and JTAG header pins (39-42, usable
// as plain GPIO when not actively debugging). Full copy of
// variants/esp32/esp32s3/board.json otherwise.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (BUTTON_OK, active-low).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO10 tagged "button" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (BUTTON_UP, active-low).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO11 tagged "button" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (BUTTON_DOWN, active-low).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO14 tagged "button" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (BUTTON_MENU, active-low).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO15 tagged "led_high" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (LED_GREEN, active-high).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO16 tagged "led_high" - confirmed Espressif ESP32-S3-USB-OTG user guide (LED_YELLOW, active-high).
